Article 2 Where the goods or services provided by a business operator fall under any of the following circumstances, the provisions of Article 47 of the Law on Protection of Consumer Rights and Interests shall apply:
(1) The goods or services provided have defects and infringe upon the lawful rights and interests of many unspecified consumers;
(2) The goods or services provided may endanger the personal or property safety of consumers, and no true explanation or clear warning is given, and no correct methods for using the goods or receiving the services or for preventing the occurrence of hazards are indicated; or false or misleading publicity is made about information such as the quality, performance, use, and validity period of the goods or services provided;
(3) Business premises such as hotels, shopping malls, restaurants, banks, airports, stations, ports, theaters, scenic areas, sports venues, and entertainment venues have dangers endangering the personal or property safety of consumers;
(4) By means of standard terms, notices, declarations, in-store announcements, etc., unfair or unreasonable provisions are made against consumers, such as excluding or restricting consumers' rights, reducing or exempting business operators' liabilities, or increasing consumers' liabilities;
(5) Other conduct that infringes upon the lawful rights and interests of many unspecified consumers or that endangers the personal or property safety of consumers, thereby harming the public interest.

Article 4 To initiate consumer civil public interest litigation, the following materials shall be submitted:
(1) A statement of complaint conforming to the provisions of Article 121 of the Civil Procedure Law, with copies submitted according to the number of defendants;
(2) Preliminary evidence that the defendant's conduct infringes upon the lawful rights and interests of many unspecified consumers or endangers the personal or property safety of consumers, thereby harming the public interest;
(3) Proof materials that the consumer organization has performed its public welfare duties with respect to the matters involved in the litigation in accordance with the provisions of Item 4 or Item 5 of Article 37 of the Law on Protection of Consumer Rights and Interests.
